{"nodes": [{"id": "_github_workflows_integration_brokers_integration_brokers_workflow", "label": "integration-brokers workflow", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".github/workflows/integration-brokers.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seventeen live-broker suites in Docker, matrix-parallel so wall clock equals the slowest suite rather than the sum. Nightly at 03:30 UTC, offset from integration.yml's 03:00 so the two do not fight for the same runner pool; the nightly catches upstream-image regressions, since each suite tracks :latest for its broker on purpose."}, {"id": "_github_workflows_integration_brokers_broker_job", "label": "broker matrix job", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".github/workflows/integration-brokers.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "fail-fast: false so a single broker regression does not mask the others. The matrix now carries only the display label, the one thing nothing can derive; it is not a second source of truth, because IntegrationBrokerSuites.test.ts fails when matrix and tree disagree in either direction, so a backend added without a leg is a red test rather than a suite that silently never runs."}], "edges": [{"source": "_github_workflows_integration_brokers_integration_brokers_workflow", "target": "_github_workflows_integration_brokers_broker_job", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".github/workflows/integration-brokers.yml", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "_github_workflows_integration_brokers_integration_brokers_workflow", "target": "_github_workflows_integration_integration_workflow", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".github/workflows/integration-brokers.yml", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "_